---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PolicyHistory from '../components/PolicyHistory.astro';
import history from '../../assets/json/vh_cookies.json';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy | This is My Pattern"
  description="Cookies and browser storage used by thisismypattern.com."
  canonicalPath="/cookies/"
>
  <article class="article prose" data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">Policies</p>
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">This website does not use analytics, and its own pages and scripts do not set cookies.</p>
    </header>

    <h2>1. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      There is no cookie banner because there is nothing to consent to. The hosting provider, GitHub Pages, did not set any cookies on requests to
      this website when last checked on 27 October 2026.
    </p>

    <h2 id="browser-storage">2. Browser storage</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-labelledby="browser-storage" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Name</th>
            <th scope="col">Type</th>
            <th scope="col">When it is set</th>
            <th scope="col">Expiry</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <code>theme</code>
            </td>
            <td>Session storage</td>
            <td>Only when you use the light/dark appearance switch, to remember your choice while you browse</td>
            <td>When you close the tab</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>3. Other websites</h2>
    <p>
      Websites you choose to visit from links on this site, such as GitHub Discussions for comments, LinkedIn or X, may set their own cookies under
      their own policies.
    </p>

    <h2>4. What changed</h2>
    <p>
      Earlier versions of this website used Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager for statistics, with a cookie consent pop-up. These were removed
      in version 2.0 of this policy. Information collected by those services before their removal remains subject to Google's privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Enabling, disabling and deleting cookies</h2>
    <p>
      You can use your internet browser to automatically or manually delete cookies and site storage. For more information, please refer to the
      instructions in the Help section of your browser. This website works fully with cookies and storage disabled.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your rights with respect to personal data</h2>
    <p>
      See the <a href="/terms/">Terms and Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <PolicyHistory entries={history} source="/assets/json/vh_cookies.json" />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
